cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Running macOS 27 on x86 hardware: a progress record"
message: >-
  If you refer to these measurements, please cite this record and include the
  snapshot date and the internal revision given in data/status.json, because the
  figures change as the work continues.
type: dataset
authors:
  - given-names: "Will"
    family-names: "McGinnis"
    alias: "willmcginnis"
abstract: >-
  A progress record for an independent research project working to boot and run
  macOS 27.0.1, a release Apple ships for Apple silicon only, on x86-64 hardware
  as a virtual machine guest. Its furthest configuration so far reaches launchd's
  daemon phase and ssh logins, on a self-built kernel, with no usable desktop. It holds
  machine-readable progress tables covering a
  feature matrix by layer, the boot-path programs, the launchd job labels whose
  program paths are on 27.0.1's system volume or its Data-volume template, every
  kernel-collection entry of the furthest booted root, the patches carried to a
  third-party user-space translator, and a record of open walls and of risks
  that were accepted rather than fixed. Each progress row states whether it was
  measured or inferred, and most say how many boots or test cases it rests on.
  It contains no Apple code and no build or translation tooling.
keywords:
  - macOS
  - x86-64
  - arm64
  - virtualization
  - QEMU
  - KVM
  - binary translation
  - binary lifting
  - xnu
  - reverse engineering
license: CC0-1.0
version: "3.4.0"
date-released: "2026-11-25"

